    <string name="feature_saint_timeline_title">A missionary life</string>
    <string name="feature_saint_mission_banner_description">Illustration of Mother Cabrini welcoming travelers at a port</string>
    <string name="feature_saint_timeline_1_title">A vocation that crossed borders</string>
    <string name="feature_saint_timeline_1_text">Born in Sant\'Angelo Lodigiano, Italy, Francesca Cabrini gathered a community of consecrated women and founded, in 1880, the Missionary Sisters of the Sacred Heart of Jesus.</string>
    <string name="feature_saint_timeline_2_title">Meeting the immigrants</string>
    <string name="feature_saint_timeline_2_text">In 1889 she left for New York with her sisters. The mission grew with works of welcome, education and assistance, accompanying immigrants and people in vulnerable situations.</string>
    <string name="feature_saint_timeline_3_title">An international mission</string>
    <string name="feature_saint_timeline_3_text">Her work reached different countries, including Brazil. She made many journeys to accompany the communities and strengthen the missionary works.</string>
    <string name="feature_saint_timeline_4_title">Recognition by the Church</string>
    <string name="feature_saint_timeline_4_text">She was beatified in 1938 and canonized in 1946. In 1950, Pius XII proclaimed her heavenly patroness of emigrants.</string>
    <string name="feature_saint_legacy_eyebrow">Her legacy for the community</string>
    <string name="feature_saint_legacy_text">Welcome with dignity, serve with courage and bring hope to those on the move.</string>
